"Internal Error ()\nciteturn0view0 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/11625736/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\nL0: URL https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/abstract/document/11625736/ is not accessible via this tool.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[2606.21773] Decision-Focused Learning: When and Why Traditional Prediction Models Fail (https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.21773)\nciteturn0view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.21773\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 165\nL0: 【0†Search】 【1†Submit】 【2†Donate†info.arxiv.org】 【3†Log in】\nL1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · 【4†Advanced search】\nL5: \nL6: # Computer Science > Machine Learning\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 19 Jun 2026]\nL9: # Title:Decision-Focused Learning: When and Why Traditional Prediction Models Fail\nL10: \nL11: Authors:【5†Mo Liu】\nL12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Decision-Focused Learning: When and Why Traditional Prediction Models Fail, by Mo Liu\nL14: \nL15: 【6†View PDF】 【7†HTML (experimental)】\nL16: > Abstract:Plugging predictions of unknown parameters into downstream optimization problems, often referred to as the ``predict-then-optimize'' paradigm, has long been a standard approach in decision-making under uncertainty. However, improved predictive accuracy does not, in general, translate into improved decision quality. This disconnect has motivated growing interest in decision-focused learning (DFL) within the operations research community.\nL17: This tutorial reviews recent developments in DFL and highlights key methodological insights, with a particular focus on stochastic linear programming as the downstream decision-making problem. We discuss why several widely used tools in traditional statistical learning are not directly suited to decision-focused settings and must be rethought, including (i) data collection strategies driven purely by predictive uncertainty and (ii) distributional distance measures such as the Wasserstein distance.\nL18: We summarize properties of DFL that distinguish it from conventional predictive modeling and provide insights into the development of new decision-focused tools.\nL19: Subjects:  | Machine Learning (cs.LG); Methodology (stat.ME)\nL20: Cite as:  | 【8†arXiv:2606.21773】 [cs.LG]\nL21:    | (or 【9†arXiv:2606.21773v1】 [cs.LG] for this version)\nL22:    | 【10†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2606.21773†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Mo Liu [【11†view email】]\nL26: [v1] Fri, 19 Jun 2026 21:45:40 UTC (2,669 KB)\nL27: \nL28: Full-text links:\nL29: \nL30: ## Access Paper:\nL31: \nL32: View a PDF of the paper titled Decision-Focused Learning: When and Why Traditional Prediction Models Fail, by Mo Liu\nL33: \nL34:   * 【6†View PDF】\nL35:   * 【7†HTML (experimental)】\nL36:   * 【12†TeX Source】\nL37: \nL38: 【13†view license】\nL39: \nL40: ### Current browse context:\nL41: \nL42: cs.LG\nL43: \nL44: 【14†< prev】   |   【15†next >】\nL45: \nL46: 【16†new】 | 【17†recent】 | 【18†2026-06】\nL47: \nL48: Change to browse by:\nL49: \nL50: 【19†cs】\nL51: 【20†stat】\nL52: 【21†stat.ME】\nL53: ### References & Citations\nL54: \nL55:   * 【22†NASA ADS†ui.adsabs.harvard.edu】\nL56:   * 【23†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com】\nL57:   * 【24†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org】\nL58: \nL59: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL60: \nL61: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL62: \nL63: [Button: ×]\nL64: \nL65: loading...\nL66: \nL67: Data provided by:\nL68: \nL69: ### Bookmark\nL70: \nL71: [Input] Bibliographic Tools\nL72: # Bibliographic and Citation Tools\nL73: \nL74: [Input] Bibliographic Explorer Toggle\nL75: \nL76: Bibliographic Explorer (【25†What is the Explorer?†info.arxiv.org】)\nL77: \nL78: [Input] Connected Papers Toggle\nL7